{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "SNG",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The song of songs, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Solomon's.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth: for thy love ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better than wine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because of the savor of thy good ointments thy name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ointment poured forth, therefore do the virgins love thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Draw me, we will run after thee: the king hath brought me into his chambers; we will be glad and rejoice in thee, we will remember thy love more than wine: the upright love thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " black, but comely, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, as the tents of Kedar, as the curtains of Solomon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look not upon me, because I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " black, because the sun hath looked upon me: my mother's children were angry with me; they made me the keeper of the vineyards; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my own vineyard have I not kept.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Tell me, O thou whom my soul loveth, where thou feedest, where thou makest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy flock",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to rest at noon: for why should I be as one that turneth aside by the flocks of thy companions?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou knowest not, O thou fairest among women, go forth by the footsteps of the flock, and feed thy kids beside the shepherds tents.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have compared thee, O my love, to a company of horses in Pharaoh's chariots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy cheeks are comely with rows ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of jewels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", thy neck with chains ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of gold",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We will make for thee borders of gold with studs of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "While the king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sitteth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at his table, my spikenard sendeth forth its smell.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A bundle of myrrh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my well beloved to me; he shall lie all night betwixt my breasts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a cluster of camphor in the vineyards of En-gedi.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fair, my love; behold, thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fair; thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hast",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doves' eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fair, my beloved, yes, pleasant: also our bed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " green.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beams of our house ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cedar, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our rafters of fir.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
